<title>DENMARK: Danish Codan six-month 96 profit climbs.</title>
<headline>Danish Codan six-month 96 profit climbs.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Group ordinary pre-tax result	    443 vs 178</p>
<p> Group net result after minorities	555 vs 87</p>
<p> Gross premiums, accident		 1,798 vs 1,756</p>
<p> Gross premiums, life			 758 vs 757</p>
<p>Balance end-JUne 1996  53.66 billion vs 51.06  end-June 1995</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Denmark's second biggest insurer is A/S Forsikringsselskabet Codan. It is 71.45 percent owned by Britain's Royal &amp; Sun Alliance. It said in a statement that it forecast a better technical insurance result in 1996's second half than in its first six months.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom, 45-33-969650</p>
